WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Speaker 1: So we have a bit of a lighthearted&nbsp;
story to wrap things up today, and it has to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:10.000
with one of the worst pandemic inspired changes&nbsp;
to our society, which is of course the dreaded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.640
QR code at restaurants replacing physical menus.&nbsp;
We know that during the pandemic, businesses would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.760
try to take advantage of the situation by not&nbsp;
providing us with things that we were used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.480
and just using COVID as an excuse. Like they would&nbsp;
say, Oh, sorry, we can't clean your hotel room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:32.080
because of COVID and sorry you can't bring your&nbsp;
reusable bag to the grocery store because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:37.840
COVID. Remember that one? Well, none of these&nbsp;
changes were as bad as the dreaded QR code&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.280
scanner at restaurants. And while some of&nbsp;
the pandemic era inconveniences are no more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:49.440
the dreaded QR code at restaurants persists, and&nbsp;
the idea of introducing them in the first place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.240
was pretty clear. You don't have people touching&nbsp;
the menus that way. You don't have to sanitize the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.560
menus as often. And it's the same reason why&nbsp;
restaurants during the height of the pandemic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:04.240
got rid of the ketchup bottles on the tables and&nbsp;
the salt and pepper shakers. And it didn't take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:10.800
long for us to learn that the virus was largely&nbsp;
an airborne transmitted virus. It didn't really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.200
transfer that much from surfaces. So a lot of&nbsp;
these changes that we made were pointless and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.840
we could have backtracked on them right then&nbsp;
and there pretty early on in the pandemic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:25.200
But restaurants persisted with the QR thing&nbsp;
because printing menus can be expensive. You need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.600
to replace them sometimes when they get dirty or&nbsp;
when you change the menu. You got to think about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.800
the printing costs. And it's also in a low labor&nbsp;
environment, just better for businesses to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:40.800
the QR codes because you don't have to have staff&nbsp;
distribute and collect the menus, but customers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:48.640
absolutely revile the QR code, myself included.&nbsp;
A recent Technomic survey found that about 88% of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:54.640
respondents said that they preferred paper menus&nbsp;
to digital QR codes. About 66% of respondents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.680
agreed or strongly agreed that they didn't like QR&nbsp;
codes because they involve pulling out your phone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:05.920
as soon as you sit down at the table. About 57%&nbsp;
agreed that using QR codes felt like a chore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:12.400
and 55% agreed that QR codes were hard to read and&nbsp;
browse through. And it actually does seem to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.040
sense for restaurants to bring back the physical&nbsp;
menus now, not just because customers hate it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.480
They'll sometimes leave these awful reviews for&nbsp;
restaurants because of the QR codes. The QR codes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.440
actually are leading to. People ordering less&nbsp;
because if you have a menu left on the table,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.240
for example, sometimes it will have the pictures&nbsp;
of the food and the drinks and the desserts and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:37.120
everything. So you may be tempted to order more&nbsp;
just by giving a glance over at it and saying, Oh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:42.720
that looks good, I want to order that. Whereas if&nbsp;
you have to pull out your phone, scan the QR code,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.720
open up the website, scroll down, find what&nbsp;
you're looking for. That's more of an active&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.520
action versus a passive action of just glancing at&nbsp;
something and saying, That looks good. I want that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.200
now. Depending on my mood, I will sometimes lie at&nbsp;
the restaurant and I'll say, I don't have a phone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:02.080
or I have a flip phone, and so I need a physical&nbsp;
menu. That is something that you can try out at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:07.120
home there. They'll have a few physical menus&nbsp;
at their ready, so they're probably not going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.680
to be happy to give it to you. But you can always&nbsp;
just make up an excuse and I'm sure you'll get it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.320
And another pro-tip for dealing with the other&nbsp;
inconvenience that people absolutely hate at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:22.080
restaurants is when you're about to pay for the&nbsp;
meal, just have cash handy with the tip included&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:27.040
so that when the server comes over you can just&nbsp;
pay for it all at once. They bring you the check,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.320
you look at the amount you probably know about&nbsp;
what it's going to be. You just give them the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:35.200
cash. They go on with it. Rather than having&nbsp;
to give them a card. They leave, come back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.320
and then you fill out the tip and everything. It&nbsp;
saves you about half the headache because that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.640
one of the things that people hate most about&nbsp;
restaurants having to wait at the end of your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.640
meal when you just want to get up and leave.&nbsp;
All right. That's going to do it for today's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.880
show. My thank you to David for allowing&nbsp;
me to fill in for him today while he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

